                                "sense_id": "7628299e-abce-3187-bb5b-c92002b01b59",
                                "text": "1982, Ronald Hugh Morrieson, NZ, Predicament, The Dunmore Press, page 68,\n“Well, I don′t know what you′ll think. I′m only saying this to show what you′ve all done for me, but last Christmas dinner I had cold savs.”\nThere was silence and then Mervyn added with a break in his voice, “Saveloys. […] ”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "beab2c4b-e36a-47ad-ac57-5431eb15cd15",
                                "sense_id": "7628299e-abce-3187-bb5b-c92002b01b59",
                                "text": "‘Your turn today, Lil,’ he said. ‘Fish and chips for me. No, wait, I′ll have savs, faggots and pease pudding.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2ded757-8352-4a0a-8621-47c0647a305e",
                                "sense_id": "7628299e-abce-3187-bb5b-c92002b01b59",
                                "text": "The menu of the average fish and chip shop will also offer[…]battered savs/Pluto pups (these are basically saveloy sausages with a fried batter on a stick, dipped in tomato ketchup) as well as a choice of homemade marinated pickles."
                            }
